# Lesson 5, new exercise: Stayman over a 2NT opening, no fit.
title: Stayman over 2NT: no fit
id: L05-16
type: exercise
lesson: 5
concepts: 5.7
student: S
board: 33
dealer: N
vulnerable: none

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  KQ2    AK8    AKJ2   Q98
  E  T983   JT     984    AJT4
  S  654    Q943   T73    K76
  W  AJ7    7652   Q65    532

auction:
  N 2NT    = 21-22 points, balanced
  E Pass
  S 3C*    = Stayman: do you have a 4-card major?
     key: Four hearts and 5 points: enough to look for a heart game.
     not Pass: 5 points opposite 21-22 is enough for game.
     not 3NT: You have four hearts. Check for a fit first.
  W Pass
  N 3D     = No 4-card major
  E Pass
  S 3NT*   = No fit, so game in no-trump
     key: Partner has no 4-card major, so settle in 3NT.
     not 4H: Partner has denied four hearts.
     not Pass: 3♦ only says "no major." It is not a place to play.
  W Pass
  N Pass
  E Pass

auction recap:
  With four hearts you asked first. Partner's 3♦ said "no major," so there was
  no heart fit and you bid the no-trump game. North is declarer, because North
  bid no-trump first, and so East will lead to the first trick.

play:
  1   E CJ  S C6  W C2  N CQ
  2   N HA  E HT  S H3  W H2
      note: Start on the hearts, the long suit: four of them will be winners.
  3   N HK  E HJ  S H4  W H5
      note: Keep cashing hearts.
  4   N H8  E S3  S H9  W H6
      note: Dummy wins, and the hearts are now good.
  5   S HQ  W H7  N S2  E C4
      note: Cash dummy's good ♥Q.
  6   S DT  W D6  N D2  E D4
      note: Lead toward declarer's A-K-J: if West has the queen, the ten wins.
  7   S D7  W D5  N DJ  E D8
      note: Lead another diamond, finessing the jack.
  8   N DA  E D9  S D3  W DQ
      note: Cash the ♦A, and the queen falls.
  9   N DK  E S8  S S4  W C3
      note: The ♦K too.
  10  N C9  E CT  S CK  W C5
      note: Lead toward dummy's ♣K to set up a club trick.
  11  S S6  W S7  N SQ  E S9
      note: Lead toward declarer's ♠K-Q.
  12  N C8  E CA  S C7  W SJ
      note: Exit with a club.
  13  E ST  S S5  W SA  N SK
      note: 11 tricks: 3NT made with two overtricks.

play recap:
  Declarer's plan: take the heart tricks, then set up the diamonds with a
  finesse.

  3NT made 11 tricks. Passing 2NT would have scored only a part-score, and
  4♥ was never on: partner had just three hearts. Stayman found out there
  was no fit, and 3NT was the right game.
